Close a task's `execute_tool` span when its terminal `task_updated` arrives after
the tool_result that was ignored as a launch receipt. The rule was that a terminal
update stops treating the receipt as untrustworthy so whichever signal arrives
next closes the span, but live the ordering is the other way round — measured in a
recorded session the receipt lands at 9.7s and the terminal update at 36.4s — so
there is no next signal, and the SDK documents terminal tasks whose notification
is suppressed entirely. The span leaked to teardown and closed after the following
chat spans with no status. The close waits one message so the `task_notification`
that usually lands on the same millisecond, and which carries the task's real
output, still gets to supply it.
